
LMS-PROJECT Backend - API Documentation

Overview
This document describes the user-related REST API endpoints in the lms-backend. All endpoints are JSON-based. Authentication uses JWT in the Authorization header as: Bearer <token>.

Base URL
- Local: http://localhost:PORT/api (replace PORT with your server port)

Endpoints

1) Create User
- POST /users
- Description: Register a new user.
- Body (application/json):
	{
		"name": "string",
		"email": "user@example.com",
		"password": "string"
	}
- Success (201):
	{
		"success": true,
		"message": "User created successfully",
		"user": { "id": number, "name": "string", "email": "string" }
	}
- Errors: 400 for validation or if user already exists.

2) Login User
- POST /auth/login (or /login depending on route setup)
- Description: Authenticate user and receive JWT token.
- Body (application/json):
	{
		"email": "user@example.com",
		"password": "string"
	}
- Success (200):
	{
		"success": true,
		"message": "Login successful",
		"token": "<jwt>"
	}
- Errors: 401 for invalid credentials.

3) Get Users (Admin / List)
- GET /users
- Description: Fetch paginated list of users with optional search, filtering and sorting.
- Query params:
	- page (number, default 1)
	- limit (number, default 10)
	- search (string) — searches name and email (case-insensitive)
	- sortby (string) — currently supported id
	- sortorder (string) — asc or desc
	- role (string) — filter by role
- Success (200):
	{
		"success": true,
		"pagination": {
			"totalUsers": number,
			"currentPage": number,
			"totalPages": number,
			"limit": number
		},
		"filters": { "search": "", "sortby": "id", "sortorder": "desc", "role": "" },
		"users": [ { "id": number, "name": "string", "email": "string", "role": "string" }, ... ]
	}

4) Get Profile
- GET /users/me (or /profile depending on route setup)
- Description: Get authenticated user's profile. Requires Authorization header.
- Headers:
	- Authorization: Bearer <token>
- Success (200):
	{
		"success": true,
		"user": { "id": number, "name": "string", "email": "string" }
	}
- Errors: 401 if token missing/invalid; 404 if user not found.

Error Handling
- API returns HTTP status codes and JSON error messages. Common responses: 400 (bad request), 401 (unauthorized), 404 (not found), 500 (server error).

Notes
- Passwords are stored hashed (bcrypt).
- JWT secret must be set in environment: JWT_SECRET
- Adjust route paths to match your router configuration (examples above follow common conventions).

Contact
- Repository: check project root for README and route configuration for exact paths.
